    structure: |
      . T T .      corners = bg, interior = bg
      L . . R      each side = (N-2) cells of one solid color
      L . . R      4 sides use 4 distinct non-bg colors
      . B B .
    position: near grid center (solver picks candidate closest to center)
    edge_len: N-2 (= 2 when N=4)
  src (sprites):
    count: 2-4 matching sprites + 0-1 distractors
    matching: one monochrome sprite per hub-edge color; color uniquely pairs sprite to side
    missing_sides: 0-2 sides may have no sprite (only hub edge shown, nothing added in output)
    connectivity: 8-connected (may be only diag-connected; solver uses 8-conn labeling)
    symmetry: in attached orientation, sprite is symmetric perpendicular to contact axis (fliplr for top/bot attach, flipud for left/right attach); required by solver
    contact_edge: exactly N-2 contiguous filled cells on the attachment side of the rotated sprite
    rotation: solver tries rot90 x 0-3; exactly 1 rotation should be valid (avoid rotationally symmetric shapes that create ambiguity)
    pixels: 4-12 [observed], bbox height 2-4, width 2-6 [observed]
    placement: scattered far from hub and each other (Chebyshev gap >= 3 [observed])
    orientation: placed in a random rotation different from the attached orientation
    distractors: 0-1 sprites in a non-edge color; ignored by solver, absent from output
  output:
