    - Pick grid H, W, hub size N (use 4), bg color (8)
    - Choose 4 distinct non-bg colors for hub edges; place hub near center with margin >= max sprite extent + 2 on all sides
    - Choose K sides (2-4) to get sprites; for each side, design a monochrome sprite mask satisfying the symmetry and contact-edge constraints, ensuring exactly 1 valid rotation
    - Build output by attaching each sprite flush against its hub side; verify no overlap between attached sprites
    - Derive input by detaching each sprite, applying a random non-identity rotation, and placing it at a random location with Chebyshev gap >= 3 from hub and other sprites
    - Optionally add 0-1 distractor sprite in a fresh non-edge color
